  given: the agent's Chat beside the interviewee's profile panel, with a scripted model
  when: Rich introduces himself, states two goals, names the blocker, confirms both goals
  then:
    - the Goals region lists both goals and reads "Confirmed" twice
    - the Facts region lists the recorded facts
    - the space holds one Person and two confirmed goals, and the agent's brain at least three facts
```

```mdl
scenario T-9: A watch is delivered where it was set   # triggers.test.ts
  # covers [F-6.2]
  given: Kai with two watches on Dima, one set in Kai's space and one through Kai in another space
  when: a fact of Dima's is pushed in Kai's space
  then:
    - only the watch set here fires, and its recipient gets one update
    - the other watch's wake stays queued for its own space
    - an agent delivers a watch in the space it was set from, and its home delivers one stored without an origin
```

```mdl
scenario T-10: An agent is admitted to a space as a member   # admit-agent.test.ts
  # covers [F-7.2, F-7.3]
  given: a space owned by someone else
  then:
    - the agent's identity is admitted as an editor, named after the agent
    - a space's owner and admins may admit it and an editor may not; in a locked space no one may, its owner included
    - a current member is left as it is, and one that was removed is admitted again
    - a space that refuses the admission fails it with AdmitAgentError
    - for the agent's creator, missingJoin names the step a failed join left undone: the membership, the admission, or both; nothing when both happened
    - missingJoin names nothing for anyone but the creator, for an agent without a DID or its records, for an agent an admin removed, or where the creator may not admit it, as in a locked space
```

```mdl
scenario T-11: Agent identities follow the setting   # create-agent.test.ts
  # covers [F-7.4]
  given: the plugin's setting off, as by default, and an EDGE that answers provisioning
  when: an agent is created, then another with the setting on
  then:
    - the first has no DID and EDGE was asked nothing
    - the second takes the DID EDGE answered with, from one provisioning request
```

```mdl
scenario T-12: Agent spaces list their admins   # AgentSpace.test.ts
  # covers [F-7.5, F-7.6, F-7.8]
  given: an agent space owned by the agent, with an admin, an editor and a reader; an agent space the identity was removed from; an untagged space
  then:
    - agentOf is the owner, and the admins are the admin and the editor, not the reader
    - the identity administers only the first space, and a reader of it none
    - administeredAgents reads the name, DID, identity key and home URI an open agent space records, and only the DID and identity key of one still opening
```

```mdl
scenario T-13: An invited agent keeps one brain   # invite-agent.test.ts
  # covers [F-6.1, F-8.1, F-8.2, F-8.3, F-8.5]
  given: Kai in a home space; a fact Mykola stated in Kai's home brain
  when: Kai is invited into a second space twice, then as its presence into a third, then back home; the presence recalls and learns
  then:
    - one presence exists, keyed to Kai's URI, with Kai's name, DID and instructions; back home Kai itself is returned
    - every presence names Kai's brain; the presence's chat is empty
    - op:retrieveMemories in the presence's space returns the home fact, said by Mykola
    - a fact the presence reads lands in the home brain, and the Brain companion lists both
    - only an admitted agent the member administers is put to work, by the home its own space records, and never in that space
    - an admin who cannot reach Kai's home invites it from what Kai's space records: a presence keyed to Kai's URI with its name, its DID and the base instructions; inviting again returns it
```

```mdl
scenario T-14: An admin's client adds the agent's admins on EDGE   # agent-admin-sync.test.ts
  # covers [F-7.9]
  given: Kai's space with Kai as its owner, the identity as an admin, an editor and a reader; an EDGE that minted Kai
  when: the sync runs, again unchanged, then after the editor is removed and another member joins as an editor
  then:
    - the first run adds the admin and the editor, not the reader, after EDGE names the space as Kai's
    - an unchanged space sends nothing; the change adds the newcomer and sends nothing for the removed editor
    - a space EDGE names as another, or where EDGE counts the identity a contact, sends nothing but the check
    - an add EDGE answered with 404 is not sent again; one that failed with 503 is, and the pass asks to run again
    - EDGE answering 503 when the space is to be confirmed asks for a retry; a 403, or an agent EDGE does not know, does not
    - a pass that asked for a retry runs again 30 seconds later without a wake; one that did not waits for a wake
```

## Not built

Design items from `docs/DESIGN.md` and `docs/FACTS.md` that this package does not implement:

- The EDGE gateway Durable Object and the agent turn on EDGE live outside this package (EDGE repo).
  Until edge step 4 the gateway still reads a `DiscordBinding` and calls `ensureThreadChat`, neither of
  which exists any more, so Discord conversations do not reach the agent.
- The intended shape: an agent is a member of the spaces it is invited to, and people talk to it there as a
  bot in their chats. As built, an agent with an identity is a member of each shared space it is in (F-7.2), but
  people talk to it through a presence (an `Agent` keyed to its home), in a private chat of their own in each
  space (F-8.4); its messages carry no identity (`sender` is `{ role: 'assistant' }`); and chats in a space do
  not wake the agent.
- Removing an agent from a space's members leaves its presence there and the space registered with its brain.
- Goals are objects in the space they were recorded in; only facts are shared through the brain.
- Runtime-assembled knowledge context at the start of each turn; consolidation (dedupe, promotion of
  inferred facts); editing or retracting single facts in the UI (Reset wipes the brain).
- Required provenance: a recorded fact's `source` is optional as built.
- Linking an entity the extractor could not resolve to the object it names later (`owl:sameAs`):
  facts read before a Person existed keep their slug, which recall still matches by name.
- The interview checklist on `Chat.tasks`: the skill uses a checklist only if a tool for it is bound.

## QA

Executable tests. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by test and step number.

```mdl
test QA-1: Create an autonomous agent, give it a Discord channel, start the bot
  desc: |
    The primary journey: an agent from Settings › Agents, a Discord-backed channel picked as one of
    its channels, and the bot control round-trip to EDGE through plugin-thread's generic channel
    operations. Run against a local EDGE with a deliberately invalid bot token, so the gateway cannot
    connect and the status must carry the gateway's error — a "Connected" banner here is a defect.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-1.1, F-3.1, F-3.3]
  status: unverified         # never run against the app
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open and SPACE_READY
    - plugin-agent and plugin-discord are enabled (both are tagged labs) and Composer points at a local EDGE
    - no Agent named "QA: Interlocutor $runId" exists
  before:
    - name: Add a bot token
      do: Add an access token with source "discord.com", account "QA: bot $runId" and value "qa-invalid-token".
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.addObject { object: { "@type": "org.dxos.type.accessToken", source: "discord.com", account: "QA: bot $runId", token: "qa-invalid-token" } }
      capture: token
      expect: the token exists in the space
    - name: Create a Discord channel
      do: |
        Create a channel named "QA: discord $runId" with the Discord backend: Bot token "QA: bot $runId",
        Application ID "qa-app-$runId", channel "qa-channel-$runId".
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.thread.createChannel { spaceId: $given.space.id, name: "QA: discord $runId", kind: "org.dxos.channel.backend.discord", options: { accessToken: Ref($token.object), applicationId: "qa-app-$runId", channels: ["qa-channel-$runId"] } }
      capture: channel
      expect: the channel exists and its properties show the Discord form and a bot status banner
  steps:
    - name: Create the agent
      do: |
        Open the space's Settings › Agents, type "QA: Interlocutor $runId" beside Add agent, and click
        Add agent.
      invoke: [op:createAgent] { name: "QA: Interlocutor $runId" }
      capture: agent
      expect: the agent appears in Settings › Agents with that name
    - name: Give the agent the channel
      do: Open the agent's Activity companion and pick "QA: discord $runId" under Channels.
      expect: |
        the Discord form, the bot status banner and the Start/Stop/Refresh toolbar appear under the
        picker, and "Conversations" reads "No channel conversations yet."
      note: NO `invoke` — the container saves AgentChannels with `db.add`. This step is why the test is `actors: human`.
    - name: Start the bot
      do: Click Start bot.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.thread.connectChannel { channel: Ref($channel.object) }
      expect: the toolbar is briefly disabled, then the banner shows a gateway state other than Connected
      assert: return $result.status.state !== 'ready' && $stepErrors.length === 0
      note: An invocation failure (EDGE not running) means the fixture is wrong — report the step as blocked.
    - name: Read the status
      do: Click Refresh status.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.thread.getChannelStatus { channel: Ref($channel.object) }
      expect: the banner reads "Failed" (or "Connecting" while EDGE retries) and shows the gateway's error; never "Connected"
      assert: return $result.status.state !== 'ready' && typeof $result.status.error === 'string'
  after:
    - name: Stop the bot
      do: Click Stop bot (if enabled).
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.thread.disconnectChannel { channel: Ref($channel.object) }
      expect: the banner reads Stopped or Disconnected
    - name: Delete the agent, channel and token
      do: Delete "QA: Interlocutor $runId", the "QA: discord $runId" channel and the "QA: bot $runId" token.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [Obj($agent.agent), Obj($channel.object), Obj($token.object)] }
      expect: none of them remains; the agent's channel list and chats go with it (they are its children)
```

```mdl
test QA-2: Interview a person and confirm their goals
  desc: |
    The interview skill against a live model: the agent resolves the interviewee, records facts
    and proposes goals while the conversation runs, and confirming the read-back flips the goals to
    Confirmed in the Person's properties. The deterministic counterpart is the storybook play
    `stories-assistant` › Interview › TestInterviewScripted (scenario T-8), which scripts the model;
    it is a story, not a Playwright spec, so it is not listed under `automated:`.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-5.1, F-5.2, F-5.3, F-4.6]
  status: unverified         # pending — needs a live model key; never run against the app
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open and SPACE_READY
    - plugin-agent is enabled
    - a live model is available to the assistant (an Anthropic API key, or the EDGE AI service) — ABORT
      without one; a scripted model is the storybook's job, not this test's
    - no Person whose fullName contains "QA-$runId" exists
    - person: the Person the agent resolves in step 2 — resolved by the runner after that step as the
      one `org.dxos.type.person` whose fullName contains "QA-$runId"; the model creates it, so there is
      no invocation to `capture` it from
  before:
    - name: Create the interviewer
      do: In Settings › Agents, type "QA: Interviewer $runId" beside Add agent and click Add agent.
      invoke: [op:createAgent] { name: "QA: Interviewer $runId" }
      capture: agent
      expect: the agent appears in Settings › Agents
  steps:
    - name: Open the agent's chat
      do: Click "QA: Interviewer $runId", then open its chat in the Assistant companion.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.appToolkit.open { subject: ["root/$given.space.id/ai/org.dxos.type.agent/$agent.agent.objectId"] }
      expect: an empty chat with the agent is ready for input
    - name: Introduce yourself
      do: Send "Hi, I am Quinn QA-$runId."
      expect: |
        the agent states the purpose of the interview in a sentence and asks one open question; the
        trace shows a resolveEntity call
      note: NO `invoke` — the model chooses the tool calls. Human-only.
    - name: State two goals
      do: |
        Send "I want the QA demo working by Friday, and to hire one designer this year." Answer any
        follow-up question briefly until the agent reads the goals back and asks you to confirm them.
      expect: |
        each turn asks one question and reflects back what it heard; the read-back names both goals
      note: NO `invoke` — model-driven.
    - name: See the proposed goals and facts
      do: Open Quinn's Properties panel.
      invoke: [op:retrieveFacts] { subject: Ref($given.person) }
      capture: proposed
      expect: |
        the panel has a "Goals" region listing the two goals, each "Proposed", and a "Facts" region
        with at least one fact marked Stated
      assert: |
        return $result.goals.length >= 2
          && $result.goals.every((goal) => goal.status === 'proposed')
          && $result.facts.length > 0;
      note: Scoped to `$given.person`, whose name carries `$runId`, so goals left by an earlier run cannot count.
    - name: Confirm the goals
      do: Send "Yes, both are right."
      expect: the agent says it confirmed the goals and summarises what it recorded
      note: NO `invoke` — model-driven.
    - name: See the goals confirmed
      do: Look at Quinn's Properties panel again, without reopening it.
      invoke: [op:retrieveFacts] { subject: Ref($given.person) }
      capture: final
      expect: every goal in the Goals region now reads "Confirmed", and the same goals are listed
      assert: |
        const titles = (goals) => goals.map((goal) => goal.title).sort().join('\n');
        return $result.goals.length === $proposed.goals.length
          && titles($result.goals) === titles($proposed.goals)
          && $result.goals.every((goal) => goal.status === 'confirmed');
      note: The panel must update in place (F-5.3); a refresh only after reopening is a failure of this step.
  after:
    - name: Delete the interview's goals and facts
      do: Delete the goals listed in Quinn's properties, and reset the interviewer's knowledge.
      invoke: |
        org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: $final.goals.map((row) => Obj(row.goal)) };
        org.dxos.operation.agent.resetBrain { agent: Ref($agent.agent) }
      expect: Quinn's properties read "Nothing recorded yet."
      note: Facts live in the agent's brain, so they are wiped with it rather than removed from the space.
    - name: Delete the person
      do: Delete Quinn.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [Obj($given.person)] }
      expect: no Person whose fullName contains "QA-$runId" remains; the profile document goes with it (it is a child)
    - name: Delete the interviewer
      do: Right-click "QA: Interviewer $runId" and choose Delete agent.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [Obj($agent.agent)] }
      expect: the agent and its chat leave the navtree
```

```mdl
test QA-3: Two people, one agent — a watch fires across private chats
  desc: |
    Two members, each on their own device and HALO identity, talk to the same agent in their own
    private chats. One asks to be kept posted on the other's work; when the other says what they are
    working on, the agent reads it into its brain, the watch wakes, and the update reaches the first
    member's chat. Facts live only in the agent's brain (BrainService), never in ECHO, so the Brain
    companion's Facts tab is the only place they show.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-1.1]
  status: unverified         # needs a live model and an EDGE that hosts the agent's chats and brain
  given:
    - two devices, each with its own identity: Alice (host) and Bob (guest), display names set
    - plugin-agent is enabled on both (it is tagged labs)
    - Composer points at an EDGE that runs agent chats (`Agent.chatLocation` is `edge` for an agent's chat)
      and serves a live model — ABORT without one
  steps:
    - name: Alice creates a space and an agent
      do: Alice creates a space "Launch room", then clicks Add agent in its Settings › Agents.
      invoke: [op:createAgent] { name: "" }
      capture: agent
      expect: the agent appears in Settings › Agents and its article opens Alice's private chat
    - name: Alice invites Bob; Bob joins
      do: Alice opens Members, creates a single-use invitation; Bob joins with the code and the auth code.
      expect: Bob's navtree shows "Launch room" with the same agent under Agents
    - name: Each opens a private chat with the agent
      do: Both click the agent under Agents.
      expect: |
        each sees an empty chat ready for input; neither sees the other's conversation (each chat is the
        member's own participant chat, hosted on EDGE)
      note: NO `invoke` — the article opens the viewer's chat through op OpenPrivateChat with their identity DID.
    - name: Alice asks to be kept posted on Bob
      do: Alice sends "Keep me posted on what Bob is working on."
      expect: the agent acknowledges; the Brain companion's Goals tab lists Alice's goal with a watch on Bob
      note: NO `invoke` — the model chooses watchFacts.
    - name: Bob says what he is working on
      do: Bob sends "I'm working on the indexer migration this week."
      expect: the agent replies to Bob
      note: NO `invoke` — model-driven; the end-request hook (runTriggers) reads the turn into the brain.
    - name: Alice receives the update
      do: Watch Alice's chat, without sending anything.
      expect: a message from the agent appears in Alice's chat telling her Bob is working on the indexer migration
      note: A watch whose update never reaches Alice's chat is a failure of this step, not of the model.
    - name: The facts are in the brain
      do: Open the agent's Brain companion and its Facts tab.
      expect: |
        the Facts tab lists a fact that Bob works on the indexer migration, attributed to Bob; no
        annotation object holds it in the space
```

```mdl
test QA-5: Two admins — Bob, made Kai's admin by Alice, adds Kai to his own space, where it recalls what Alice told it
  desc: |
    An agent's admins are the members who can edit its own space. Alice turns on the plugin's "Create identities for
    agents" setting and adds an agent in her space's Settings › Agents, which mints its identity and its own space on
    EDGE and joins her space as a member; she adds Bob to the agent's space the way she would add him to any space, and
    both find the agent in Profile › Agents. Alice then tells the agent about the team offsite, and Bob, who cannot
    reach Alice's space, adds the agent to his own space from its Members panel and asks it what is planned: it answers
    from its brain. The autocue flow `autocue/agent-identities.mjs` walks it side by side, one browser per person.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-1.4, F-6.1, F-7.1, F-7.2, F-7.3, F-7.4, F-7.5, F-7.7, F-7.8, F-8.1, F-8.4, F-8.6]
  status: passing             # 2026-10-15, recorded by autocue/agent-identities.mjs against local EDGE (dxos/edge#1313); steps 4 and 7 changed on 2026-10-19 and have not been re-recorded
  given:
    - alice: an identity with the display name "Alice", on one device
    - bob: an identity with the display name "Bob", on another device
    - home: Alice's own space "Studio"
    - other: Bob's own space "Offsite team"
    - plugin-agent is enabled for both; Bob has its "Create identities for agents" setting on (Settings › Plugins › Agent), and Alice turns hers on in step 1
    - EDGE with brain identities (`POST /compute/brain`) is reachable — ABORT without it
    - a live model is available to the assistant (EDGE's AI service) — ABORT without one
  steps:
    - name: Alice turns on agent identities
      do: In Alice's window open Settings › Plugins › Agent and turn on "Create identities for agents".
      expect: the switch is on; agents created from now on get identities (F-7.4)
    - name: Alice creates an agent named Kai
      do: In Alice's space open Settings › Agents, type "Kai" beside Add agent and click it.
      invoke: [op:createAgent] { name: "Kai" }, then [op:ensureIdentity] { agent: Ref($agent.agent), mint: true }
      capture: agent
      expect: Kai's chat opens at once, and a space named Kai appears in Alice's space list once EDGE has minted it
    - name: Alice sees Kai among her space's members
      do: In Alice's space open Settings › Members.
      expect: the members list Kai beside Alice
      note: Kai is admitted once EDGE has minted its identity (op:ensureIdentity), so the row can follow its space by a few seconds.
    - name: Alice finds Kai in Profile › Agents
      do: Open Alice's profile and its Agents panel, listed after the account's other panels.
      expect: Kai is listed as the contacts book lists people, with a chip for its own space and one for Alice's space
    - name: Alice invites Bob into Kai's space
      do: Click Kai's space chip on its row; in Kai's space open Settings › Members and invite one person.
      expect: an invitation code is ready to share
    - name: Bob joins Kai's space
      do: In Bob's window click + ("Add space"), choose Join, enter the invitation code and then the PIN.
      expect: Bob's space list shows Kai
    - name: Bob finds Kai in Profile › Agents
      do: Open Bob's profile and its Agents panel.
      expect: Kai is listed, so Bob administers it
    - name: Alice tells Kai about the team offsite
      do: In Alice's space open Kai and send "Hi Kai, I'm Alice. Our team offsite is in Lisbon on November 14, for 12 people, and Dima is booking the venue."
      expect: Kai acknowledges the place, the date and the headcount in a short reply
      note: NO `invoke` — the model replies on EDGE; the turn's facts are read into Kai's brain after it.
    - name: Alice adds the budget
      do: Send "The budget is 8,000 euros, and flights are still open."
      expect: Kai acknowledges the budget
      note: NO `invoke` — model-driven.
    - name: Bob adds Kai to his own space from its Members panel
      do: In Bob's window open Offsite team, then Settings › Members; under "Add from contacts" pick Kai and click Add.
      invoke: [op:inviteAgent] { agent: Ref($agent.agent) }   # run in $given.other, as Bob, after the admission
      expect: the picker lists Alice and Kai, each once; after Add, Offsite team lists Kai under Settings › Agents and among its members
      note: Bob is not a member of Alice's space, where Kai lives; Kai is Bob's contact through Kai's own space, which records its home (F-7.8), and EDGE accepts the space because Bob is Kai's admin (F-8.6).
    - name: Bob opens Kai in Offsite team
      do: Open Kai from Offsite team's Settings › Agents.
      expect: Bob's own chat with Kai opens, empty; Alice's conversation stays in her space
    - name: Bob asks Kai about the offsite
      do: Send "Check your memory: what do we have so far for the offsite?"
      expect: |
        Kai calls Recall and answers from its brain with what Alice told it, naming her: at least Lisbon,
        November 14, 12 people and the 8,000 euro budget
      note: NO `invoke` — model-driven; these words were never said in Offsite team. On 2026-10-15 Kai answered "Here's what we have for the offsite: it's in Lisbon on November 14 for 12 people, budget is €8,000, and flights are still open/unbooked. Dima is handling the venue booking. (Alice shared these details on Oct 15.)"
  after:
    - name: Remove Kai from Offsite team and Bob from Kai's space
      do: In Offsite team's Settings › Agents delete Kai; in Kai's space open Settings › Members and remove Bob.
      expect: Offsite team no longer lists Kai, and Bob's Agents panel no longer lists Kai
      note: Bob stays Kai's admin on EDGE, since admins are only added (F-7.9); his panel lists the agent spaces he is in.
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: A member has one private chat with an agent in a space. An open that starts while another is still making that chat waits for it, and of two chats made at once the article opens the one with the latest message.
  date: 2026-10-19
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [F-1.5]
  why: Reopening an agent within the two seconds its first open takes made a second chat, and after a reload the article opened the empty one, so the member's conversation looked lost.
  rejected:
    - A lock inside `ensureParticipantChat`: the second open starts in the article, and a lock would leave chats already duplicated opening the empty one.
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14082
```

```mdl
decision D-2: A member who sees the same conversation with an agent in each space the agent is in has hit a bug, which is to be reproduced and fixed.
  date: 2026-10-19
  by: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [F-8.4]
```

```mdl
decision D-3: Opening an agent in a space opens the member's private chat with it in that space, a conversation the agent's other spaces do not show, and what the agent knows stays shared through its one brain. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-19
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [F-8.4]
  why: The article opened the private chat of the agent's home whichever space it was opened from. A chat per space removes the shared conversation, and the brain every presence names keeps the agent's knowledge whole across spaces (F-6.1).
  rejected:
    - One conversation per member, shown in every space the agent is in: the behaviour reported as the bug.
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14074
```

```mdl
decision D-4: An agent's admins are credentials in the agent's own HALO, one admin per credential, added one at a time. No credential lists the admins, and none supersedes another.
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [ensureIdentity, F-7.1, F-7.9]
  why: Superseding a list is not how the HALO records facts.
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14084
```

```mdl
decision D-5: No credential revokes an agent's admin for now.
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [F-7.1, F-7.9]
  why: Space membership has no revocation yet either.
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14084
```

```mdl
decision D-6: The credential is `dxos.halo.credentials.IdentityAdmin { identity_key, admin_key }`: the agent's identity issues it, and the admin is its subject. Fills in [D-4].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [ensureIdentity, F-7.1, F-7.9]
  why: The product, EDGE and Composer already call these identities admins, and the shape matches `IdentityRecovery { identity_key, recovery_key }`, which an identity also issues into its own HALO.
  rejected:
    - `IdentityController`: the W3C DID term, but no DXOS DID document has a `controller` field, and in this codebase the word means UI and stream controllers.
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14084
```

```mdl
decision D-7: An admin's client only asks EDGE to add admins, never to take one off, so a member made a reader or removed stays the agent's admin. It sends each add once a session and again after a failure, since EDGE appends no second credential for an admin. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-20
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [F-7.9, T-14]
  why: Without revocation there is nothing to send for a removal, and resending an add repairs a credential that never reached the agent's HALO.
  rejected:
    - Delisting readers and removed members (`DELETE /compute/brain/:did/admins/:identityKey`): EDGE no longer has the route, since an admin's credential cannot be revoked.
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14084
```

```mdl
decision D-8: The account's Agents panel lists agents the way the contacts book lists people, and no longer lists each agent's admins.
  date: 2026-10-19
  by: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [AgentsPanel, F-7.7, QA-5]
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14076
```

```mdl
decision D-9: The Agents panel builds its own list in the contacts book's style rather than reusing `ContactList` directly, with a TODO to factor the two out and reconcile them. Fills in [D-8].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [AgentList, AgentsPanel]
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14076
```

```mdl
decision D-10: `AgentList` takes the agents as the contacts they are and copies `ContactList`'s rows, its markup and styles included, so the two panels look the same until they are factored out. Its space chips take the colour hashed from each space's id, as the contacts book's chips do. Fills in [D-9].
  date: 2026-10-22
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [AgentList, F-7.7]
  why: A copy of the rows keeps the panels identical without widening `@dxos/shell`'s API for one caller.
  rejected:
    - Passing each space's own colour to the chips: the space colour fix (dxos/dxos#14075) keeps every chip and the sidebar on the hash of the space id instead.
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/14076
```

